$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Carbamate (-)-45. Under argon, a solution of acid (-)-3 (24.6 mg, 36.9
μmol, azeotropically dried with benzene) in anhydrous acetone (3 ml) at 0
°C was treated with N,N-diisopropylethylamine (Huniq's base) (15 μL, 88.5
μmol) and isobutyl chloroformate (11 μL, 81.1 μmol), and the resultant
reaction mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 0.5 h. Sodium azide (0.62 M
solution in water, 290 μL, 0.177 mmol) was then added, and the resultant
mixture was stirred at 0 °C for additional 1.5 h. The reaction was
quenched with ice/water, the layers were separated, and the aqueous phase
was extracted with chilled ethyl acetate (3 × 10 ml). The combined
organic extracts were thoroughly dried over MgSO4, filtered, and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude acyl azide was taken up in anhydrous
toluene (4 ml) and heated at reflux for 15 min, after which
2-(trimethylsilyl)ethanol (100 μL, 0.744 mmol) was added in one portion.
The reaction mixture was refluxed further for 4 h, cooled to ambient
temperature, and concentrated in vacuo. Flash chromatography
(hexanes/ethyl acetate, 6:1) provided (-)-45 (193.0 g, 67% yield) as a
colorless oil. [α]25D -7.10 (c 0.95, CH2Cl2); IR (neat) 3379 (m), 2950
(s), 2903 (s), 2858 (s), 1713 (s), 1644 (m), 1514 (s), 1250 (s), 1059
(s), 966 (m), 836 (s), 776 (s) cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, C6D6) δ 7.61 (dd, J
