$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Added acid (400 mg, 1.25 mmol) to a flame-dried 25 mL round-bottom flask
with stir bar. Sealed and flushed with nitrogen, then added toluene
(distilled, 8 mL) and NEt3 (0.182 mL, 1.31 mmol). Added
diphenylphosphoryl azide (0.283 mL, 1.31 mmol) and stirred at rt for 90
min. Diluted with EtOAc and washed twice with water in a 60 mL separatory
funnel. Dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated down to
approximately 5 mL in a small flask. Added MgSO4 (0.4 g) to a separate
flame-dried 25 mL round-bottom flask with stir bar. Sealed, flushed with
nitrogen, and added toluene (distilled, 10 mL) and allyl alcohol (0.85
mL, 12.5 mmol). Heated the solution of allyl alcohol in an oil bath at
95°C. After waiting for this solution to reach oil bath temperature,
added the acyl azide solution dropwise via syringe pump over 1 h, along
with additional toluene to wash. Evaporated, diluted the crude with DCM
and water, separated, and washed the organics with saturated NaCl/water.
Dried over MgSO4, filtered, and evaporated down to a pale yellow oil.
Purified by flash column (approximately 2 x 17 cm silica gel, dry loaded,
eluted with 0-30% EtOAc/hexanes, to give carbamate, yield 306 mg, 65%.
Colourless oil; Rf = 0.32 (25% EtOAc/hexanes).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
