$DATUM tert-Butyl 2-{2-[(tert-Butoxycarbonyl)amino]ethyl}phenylcarbamate (14b)
Bis(acyl azide) 8 (2.37 g, 9.7 mmol) was dissolved in t-BuOH (200 mL) and
the mixture was refluxed for 12 h. The reaction was monitored by TLC.
After completion of the reaction, the solvent was removed under reduced
pressure. Chromatography of the residue on silica gel (50 g;
EtOAc-n-hexane, 1:3). Diurethane 14b; yield: 2.12 g (65%); colorless
crystals. mp 90- 92 °C. IR (KBr): 3333 (s), 2979 (m), 2934 (m), 1690 (s),
1520 (s), 1166 (s), 744 (s) cm-1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.78 (br
d, J = 7.4 Hz, 1 H, H-6), 7.43 (br s, 1 H, NH), 7.14 (dt, J = 7.2, 1.6
Hz, 1 H, H-5), 7.01 (br d, J = 6.7 Hz, 1 H, H-3), 6.93 (br t, J = 7.3 Hz,
1 H, H-4), 4.80 (br s, 1 H, NH), 3.16 (dt, J = 7.8, 6.5 Hz, 2 H, H-2'),
2.70 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 2 H), 1.45 [s, 9 H, OC(CH3)3], 1.39 [s, 9 H,
OC(CH3)3]. 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 156.7, 153.8, 136.8, 129.7,
128.7, 127.4, 123.7, 122.2, 80.0, 79.7, 41.1, 32.1, 28.4, 28.0. Anal.
Calcd for C18H28N2O4: C, 64.26; H, 8.39; N, 8.33. Found: C, 64.01; H,
8.25; N, 8.62.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM key step, Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM New synthetic methodology for construction of the
1,3,4,5-tetrahydro-2H-1,3-benzodiazepin-2-one skeleton
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Dengiz, Cagatay; Ozcan, Sevil; Sahin, Ertan; Balci, Metin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2010), (8), 1365-1370

