$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-Benzyl-4-[(N-phenylcarbamoyl)oxymethyl]-1,2,3-triazole (3a). A solution
of alcohol 1a (0.5 g, 3 mmol) and benzoyl azide (0.5 g, 3.4 mmol) in
dioxane (10 ml) was stirred at solvent reflux temperature for 2.5-3.0 h.
Solvent was evaporated and the viscous mass was washed with benzene. The
precipitate obtained was crystallized from ethanol.
1-[(Tetrazol-5-yl)methyl]-4-[(N-phenylcarbamoyl)oxymethyl]-1,2,3-triazole
(3c). From alcohol 1c (0.5 g, 2.8 mmol) and benzoyl azide (0.5 g, 3.4
mmol) in dioxane (10 ml). Empirical formula: C12H12N8O2, Found, %: C,
48.48, H, 4.19, N, 36.52, Calculated, %: C, 8.00, H, 4.00, N, 37.33, Mp,
°C: 78-81, IR spectra: ν, cm-1: 3330 (NH), 1227 (-O-), 1721 (C═O), 13C
NMR spectra, δ, ppm: 54.8 (CH2O); 58.1 (CH2); 118.6 (C, vic. triazole);
119.9 (2o-C, Ph); 124.5 (p-C, Ph); 129.2 (2m-C, Ph); 139.8 (ipso-C, Ph);
143.8 (ipso-C, vic. triazole); 154.5 (C═O); 159.3 (ipso-C, tetrazole).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The Curtius reaction in the synthesis of noncondensed polynuclear azoles
