$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for Curtius rearrangement and carbamate formation Acyl
azide 10 (10-90 mg, 0.049-0.44 mmol) was dissolved in toluene (6.9
mL/mmol) and the appropriate alcohol (15 equiv.) added. The reaction
mixture was heated at 80 °C, with stirring, under argon for 1 h and was
then cooled and washed with NaHCO3 solution (sat. aq., 10 mL/mmol). The
aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl acetate (3 x 10 mL/mmol) and the
combined organic layers washed with brine (20 mL/mmol), dried (MgSO4) and
evaporated in vacuo. (S)-Benzyl
7a-methyl-1-oxo-5,6,7,7a-tetrahydro-1H-pyrrolizin-3-ylcarbamate (19) On a
0.17 mmol scale, with benzyl alcohol as the trapping agent, carbamate 19
was obtained as an offwhite powder (30 mg, 61%) after purification by
flash chromatography (ether). Rf 0.13 (ethyl acetate); m.p. 124 °C; [α]D
25 +56.9 (c 1.0, CHCl3); νmax (KBr disc)/cm-1 2970m, 2925s, 2860m, 1749m,
1630m, 1511s, 1261s, 1210s, 1103s, 1025m, 799s, 700m; δH (500 MHz, CDCl3)
1.31 (3 H, s, C(8)H3), 1.69- 1.84 (2 H, m, C(7)H2), 1.96-2.15 (2 H, m,
C(6)H2), 3.11-3.17 and 3.26-3.31 (2 x 1 H, 2 x m, C(5)H2), 5.23 (2 H, s,
C(10)H2), 5.57 (1 H, s, C(2)H), 7.19 (1 H, s, NH), 7.37-7.41 (5 H, m,
Ph); δC (125 MHz, CDCl3) 22.7 (C(8)H3), 26.8 (C(6)H2), 32.0 (C(7)H2),
47.8 (C(5)H2), 68.5 (C(10)H2), 74.0 (C(7a)), 91.2 (C(2)H), 128.7, (Ph
CH), 128.8, (Ph CH), 128.9 (Ph CH), 134.7 (Ph C), 151.2 (C(3)), 168.7
(C(9)), 204.3 (C(1)); HRMS (ESI+) found 287.1387; C16H19N2O3 (MH+)
requires 287.1390.
