$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4,5-Bis(diethoxyphosphorylmethyl)furan-3-isocyanate (10). A solution of
1.06 g of the azide 9 in 12 mL of anhydrous toluene was gradually heated.
Gas evolution was monitored using a bubbler. Vigorous gas evolution took
place at 85-90°C, completed in 20 min. Toluene was removed on a rotary
evaporator, and the residue was kept in vacuum during 30 min (1 mmHg) at
room temperature. Yield of compound 10 0.6 g (60%), dark-yellow syrup. IR
spectrum, ν, cm-1: 2291. 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 1.22-1.29 m (12H, CH3),
3.00 br.d (2H, CH2P4, J PH = 24.0 Hz), 3.20 br.d (2H, CH2P5, J PH = 20.4
Hz), 4.00-4.10 m (8H, CH2OP) 7.18 s (1H, H2-furan). 13C NMR spectrum, δC,
ppm: 16.31 d (CH3, 3 J PC = 5.4 Hz), 21.45 d (CH2P4, 1 J PC = 142.1 Hz),
25.50 d (CH2P5, 1 J PC = 143.4 Hz), 62.42 d (CH2OP, 2 J PC = 6.6 Hz),
62.69 d (CH2OP, 2 J PC = 6.7 Hz), 106.33 t (C3-furan, 2 J PC = 3 J PC =
8.9 Hz), 125.26 (N=C=O), 125.71 (C3-furan), 137.81 (C2-furan), 141.67 t
(C5-furan, 2 J PC = 3 J PC = 11.1 Hz). 31P NMR spectrum, δP, ppm: 22.55 d
(P5), 27.33 d (P4), 5 J PP = 14.6 Hz.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 4-functionalized 2,3-bis(diethoxyphosphorylmethyl)furans
