$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-Benzyl-4-[(N-phenylcarbamoyl)oxymethyl]-1,2,3-triazole (3a). A solution
of alcohol 1a (0.5 g, 3 mmol) and benzoyl azide (0.5 g, 3.4 mmol) in
dioxane (10 ml) was stirred at solvent reflux temperature for 2.5-3.0 h.
Solvent was evaporated and the viscous mass was washed with benzene. The
precipitate obtained was crystallized from ethanol. Yield: 60%. Empirical
formula: C17H16N4O2, Found, %: C, 66.18, H, 5.39, N, 18.65, Calculated,
%: C, 66.23, H, 5.19, N, 18.18, Mp, °C: 108-110, IR spectra: ν, cm-1:
3295 (NH), 1246 (-O-), 1697 (C═O), 13C NMR spectra, δ, ppm: 52.0 (CH2,
Bn); 56.6 (CH2O); 117.5 (C, vic. triazole); 117.6 (2o-C, Ph); 122.5 (p-C,
Ph); 127.0 (p-C, Bn); 128.1 (2m-C, Ph); (ipso-C, Ph); 144.7 (ipso-C, vic.
triazole); 152.3 (C═O).
