$DATUM 71-43-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of acid 11 (408 mg, 0.728 mmol)
and Et3N (0.21 mL, 1.49 mmol) in benzene (1.5 mL) were added DPPA (0.19
mL, 0.891 mmol) and 2-trimethylsilylethanol (0.21 mL, 1.47 mmol). The
solution was heated to reflux for 12 h, cooled to r.t., and diluted with
sat. NaHCO3. The resulting mixture was extracted with EtOAc four times.
The combined extracts were dried over MgSO4 and concentrated to afford an
oil, which was purified by chromatography on silica gel (hexane-EtOAc) to
afford 13. Curtius rearrangement of 17 under the conditions mentioned
above proceeded smoothly to afford 18 in 57% yield.
