$DATUM 123-91-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-Benzyl-4-[(N-phenylcarbamoyl)oxymethyl]-1,2,3-triazole (3a). A solution
of alcohol 1a (0.5 g, 3 mmol) and benzoyl azide (0.5 g, 3.4 mmol) in
dioxane (10 ml) was stirred at solvent reflux temperature for 2.5-3.0 h.
Solvent was evaporated and the viscous mass was washed with benzene. The
precipitate obtained was crystallized from ethanol.
(1-Benzyl-4-[N-(2-phenyl-1,2,3-triazol-4-yl)carbamoyl]oxymethyl-1,2,3-triazole
(6a). From alcohol 1a (0.5 g, 2.6 mmol) and azide 5a (0.7 g, 3.3 mmol) in
dioxane (10 ml), Yield: 55%. Empirical formula: C19H17N7O2, Found, %: C,
61.02, H, 4.40, N, 26.26, Calculated, %: C, 60.80, H, 4.53, N, 26.13, Mp,
°C: 175-176, IR spectra, ν, cm-1: 3324 (NH), 1213 (-O-), 1725 (C═O), 13C
NMR spectra, δ, ppm: 53.5 (CH2, Bn); 62.9 (CH2O); 118.2 (2o-C, Ph); 118.9
(C, vic. triazole C-C); 126.5 (p-C, Ph); 127.0 (p-C, Bn); 128.3 (2o-C,
Bn); 128.9 (2m-C, Ph); 129.4 (2m-C, Bn); 131.4 (C, (ipso-C, vic. triazole
C-C); 147.6 (ipso-C, vic. triazole C-N); 154.5 (C═O).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The Curtius reaction in the synthesis of noncondensed polynuclear azoles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
