$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-Benzyl-4-[(N-phenylcarbamoyl)oxymethyl]-1,2,3-triazole (3a). A solution
of alcohol 1a (0.5 g, 3 mmol) and benzoyl azide (0.5 g, 3.4 mmol) in
dioxane (10 ml) was stirred at solvent reflux temperature for 2.5-3.0 h.
Solvent was evaporated and the viscous mass was washed with benzene. The
precipitate obtained was crystallized from ethanol.
3,4-Bis[N-(2-phenyl-1,2,3-triazol-4-yl)carbamoyl]oxymethyl-1,2,5-oxadiazole
(7). From 3,4-dihyd-roxymethyl-1,2,5-oxadiazole (2) (0.3 g, 2.3 mmol) and
azide 5a (1 g, 4.7 mmol) in dioxane (10 ml). Yield: 48%. Empirical
formula: C22H18N10O5, Found, %: C, 51.80 H, 3.72 N, 26.91, Calculated, %:
C, 52.58 H, 3.58 N, 27.88, Mp, °C: 229-231, IR spectra: ν, cm-1: 3335
(NH), 1215 (-O-), 1722 (C═O), 13C NMR spectra, δ, ppm 55.0 (2CH2O); 118.0
(4o-C, Ph); 126.8 (2C, vic. triazole); 128.3 (2p-C, Ph); 129.4 (4m-C,
Ph); 135.0 (2ipso-C, Ph); 145.4 (2ipso-C, vic. triazole); 150.6 (2C═O);
157.0 (2ipso-C, oxadiazole).
