$DATUM Step 1: To a suspension of the azide (2: 0.500 g, 0.435 mmol) in toluene
(20 mL) was added cyclohexanol (0.187 g, 0.869 mmol) and the mixture was
stirred at 90 °C for 4 hours. The reaction was concentrated and the crude
mixture was purified by flash chromatography (MeOH/DCM). 0.250 g (0.187
mmol, 43%) of the boc-protected amine.
