$DATUM Preparation of Amine 27: To a suspension of the azide (2: 0.200 g, 0.174
mmol) in toluene (10 mL) was added piperidinol (0.082 g, 0.521 mmol) and
the mixture was stirred at 90 °C for 7 hours. The reaction was
concentrated and the crude product was purified by flash chromatography
(EtOAc). 0.090 g (0.0695 mmol, 40%) of 27. 1H NMR (400 MHz, d6 -DMSO) δ
ppm 10.67 (b s, 1 H), 9.02 (d, 1 H), 8.68 (m, 2 H), 8.60 (s, 1 H),
8.48-8.42 (m, 1 H), 8.40 (d, 1 H), 8.25 (s, 1 H), 8.13 (d, 1 H), 7.54 (s,
1 H), 7.42-7.21 (m, 7 H), 6.03 (d, 1 H), 5.32-5.19 (m, 3 H), 5.17-5.07
(m, 1 H), 5.03-5.00 (m, 1 H), 4.98 (s, 2 H), 4.68-4.57 (m, 1 H), 4.28
(dd, 1 H), 3.79 (dd, 1 H), 3.39 (s, 3 H), 2.75-2.68 (m, 1 H), 2.59 (s, 3
H), 2.47 (m, 3 H), 2.22-2.14 (m, 1 H), 1.99-1.85 (m, 2 H), 1.41 -1.26 (m,
2 H), 1.24 -1.03 (m. 12 H), 0.88 (d, 3 H), 0.85 (d, 3 H). LC: Rt = 13.91
min. HRMS: m/z [M+2H]+2 640.1649, C58H66N14O9S6, calc 640.1647.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Antibacterial optimization of 4-aminothiazolyl analogues of the natural
product GE2270 A: Identification of the cycloalkylcarboxylic acids
