$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of Amine 29: To a solution of the azide (0.83 g, 0.722 mmol)
in PhMe (60 mL) was added the alcohol (175 μL, 1.44 mmol) and the
reaction mixture was heated at reflux at 75 °C for 4 hours and then
stirred at 22 °C for 4 days. 3 g of SiO2 was added and the solvents were
evaporated. The solids were purified by flash chromatography eluting with
MeOH/DCM (0-10 %). 300 mg of impure yellow solid. The solid was
repurified by HPLC, eluting with ACN/H2O, 0.1 % TFA (20-65 %) to provide
19 mg (21 %) 29, a yellow solid. MS m/z (M+2H)+ 627; LC: Rt = 13.15 min.
1H NMR (DMSO-d6 , 400 MHz) δ ppm 10.94 (s, 1 H), 10.07-9.89 (s, 1 H),
9.07-8.98 (m, 1 H), 8.74-8.63 (m, 2 H), 8.61 (s, 1 H), 8.50-8.35 (m, 2
H), 8.25 (s, 1 H), 8.18-8.06 (m, 1 H), 7.80 (s, 1 H), 7.57 (s, 1 H),
7.41-7.18 (m, 7 H), 6.04 (s, 1 H), 5.37- 5.16 (m, 3 H), 5.06-4.93 (m, 3
H), 4.56-4.43 (m, 2 H), 4.37-3.68 (m, 4 H), 3.62-3.47 (m, 3 H), 3.39 (s,
3 H), 3.31-3.15 (m, 2 H), 2.59 (s, 3 H), 2.45-2.35 (m, 2 H), 2.24-2.35
(m, 2 H), 2.24-2.09 (m, 1 H), 1.88- 1.73 (m, 1 H), 1.32-1.10 (m, 3 H),
0.96-0.78 (m, 6 H). HRMS: m/z (M+2H)+ 627.1385, C54H56N14O10S6, calc:
627.1387.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Antibacterial optimization of 4-aminothiazolyl analogues of the natural
product GE2270 A: Identification of the cycloalkylcarboxylic acids
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
