$DATUM 71-43-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(Diethoxyphosphorylmethyl)furyl-3 isocyanate (XI). A solution of 1.65 g
of acyl azide IIIc in 25 ml of benzene was refluxed for 2 h at 80°C, the
solvent was distilled off at a reduced pressure, and the residue was kept
in a vacuum (1 mm Hg) for 1 h at room temperature. 1.28 g of light brown
syrup consisting mainly of isocyanate XI. IR spectrum (CHCl3), ν, cm-1:
2276 (-N=C=O); 1297 (P=O), 1439 (CH2P), 1164 (P-O-C2H5), 1048 (P-O-C);
furan ring: 1598, 1517, 1221, 1209, 1029, 973, 786, 786, 777, 752, 743,
730. 1H NMR spectrum (CDCl3), δ, ppm: 1.290 t (CH3-ethyl, J HH 7.2 Hz),
3.185 d (CH2P, J HP 21.2 Hz), 4.088 m (CH2OP, J HH 7.2 Hz, J HP 14.4 Hz),
6.259 d (H4-furan, J HH 2 Hz), 7.234 d.d (H5-furan, J HH 2.0 Hz, J HP 2.5
Hz); δP 20.855 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement, other products also detected
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Diethoxyphosphorylmethylfurans in Curtius reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pevzner, L. M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of General Chemistry (2011), 81(1), 56-70

