$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-(Diethoxyphosphorylmethyl)furyl-3 isocyanate (IX).
5-Diethoxyphosphorylmethyl)furoyl-3 azide IIc, 0.4 g, was dissolved in 15
ml of toluene and refluxed for 70 min. After that the solvent was removed
at a reduced pressure, and the residue was kept in a vacuum (1 mm Hg) at
room temperature for 30 min. Isocyanate IX was obtained as yellowish
brown syrup. IR spectrum (CHCl3), ν, cm-1: 2274 (-N=C=O); 1304 (P=O),
1455 (CH2P), 1053 (P-O-C); furan ring: 1574, 1242, 1211, 1028, 968, 947,
751. 1H NMR spectrum (CDCl3), δ, ppm: 1.202 t (CH3-ethyl, J HH 6.6 Hz),
3.077 d (CH2P, J HP 21.6 Hz), 3.939-4.022 m (CH2OP), 6.039 d (H4-furan, J
HP 2.4 Hz), 7.628 s (H2-furan); δP 21.817 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Diethoxyphosphorylmethylfurans in Curtius reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
