$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Step 3: The material was dissolved in DCM (50
mL) and HCl gas was added to the solution for 10 min. The solution was
then sparged with nitrogen to remove excess acid. Concentration and
purification via HPLC. Preparation of compound 59: Step 1: To a solution
of thiazole acyl azide (2: 500 mg, 0.43 mmol) in toluene (100 mL) was
added (1R,2R,4R)-N-boc-1-amino-2-hydroxycylcopentatne-4-carboxylic acid
methyl ester (337 mg, 1.03 mmol). The mixture was heated to 90 °C for 5
hr and concentrated. Step 2: The boc deprotection for the synthesis of
compound 59 was performed according to the procedure described in the
synthesis of compound 40. Purification via HPLC. Product (3.8 mg) 59, as
a light yellow solid. LC/MS: m/z [M]+ 1268, Rt = 0.96 min (method 1). 1H
NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6 ) δ ppm 12.51 (br s, 1 H), 10.93 (br s, 1 H), 8.94
- 9.09 (m, 1 H), 8.63 - 8.75 (m, 2 H), 8.60 (s, 1 H), 8.36 - 8.50 (m, 2
H), 8.24 (s, 1 H), 8.04 - 8.16 (m, 2 H), 7.55 (s, 1 H), 7.18 - 7.41 (m, 7
H), 6.54 (br s, 1 H), 6.04 (br s, 1 H), 5.17 - 5.34 (m, 3 H), 5.08 - 5.17
(m, 1 H), 4.96 (s, 3 H), 4.30 (s, 1 H), 3.75-3.85 (m, 1 H), 3.37 (s, 3
H), 2.93 - 3.12 (m, 1 H), 2.68 - 2.78 (m, 1 H), 2.59 (s, 3 H), 2.47 (d, J
= 4.80 Hz, 3 H), 2.26 - 2.40 (m, 1 H), 2.08 - 2.23 (m, 1 H), 1.84 - 1.99
(m, 2 H), 1.18 - 1.32 (m, 1 H), 0.76 - 0.94 (m, 6 H). HRMS: m/z [M]+
1267.2454, C54H54N14O11S6, calc. 1267.2499.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement in stage 1, HCl gas used in stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Antibacterial optimization of 4-aminothiazolyl analogues of the natural
product GE2270 A: Identification of the cycloalkylcarboxylic acids
