$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-(Diethoxyphosphorylmethyl)furyl-2 isocyanate (VII). Acyl azide Ic, 1.3
g, was dissolved in 16 ml of toluene and refluxed with the protection
from air moisture for 1 h. After that the solvent was removed in a vacuum
of water-jet pump, and the residue was kept in a vacuum (1 mm Hg) at room
temperature for 1 h. Isocyanate VII was isolated as light brown syrup. IR
spectrum (CHCl3), ν, cm-1: 2148 (-N=C=O); 1294 (P=O), 1442 (CH2P), 1164
(P-O-C2H5), 1053 (P-O-C); furan ring: 1584, 1516, 1221, 1125, 1028, 972,
786, 751, 731. 1H NMR spectrum (CDCl3), δ, ppm: 1.301 t (CH3-ethyl, J HH
7.0 Hz), 3.139 d (CH2P, J HP 20.4 Hz), 4.094 m (CH2OP, J HH7.0 Hz, J HP
14.2 Hz), 5.772 d (H3-furan, J HH 3.6 Hz), 6.162 d.d (H4-furan, J HH 3.6
Hz, J HP 4 Hz); δP 21.880 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement, other products also detected
