$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(12E)-(7S,9R,10S)-4,9-Dihydroxy-10-methyl-7-[(2E)-N-(pentoxycarbonyl)-3-aminoprop-2-enyl]-7,8,9,10,11,14-hexahydro-6-oxa-benzocyclodecen-5-one
(50). A solution of acyl azide 40 (10.0 mg; 0.0163 mmol) and 1-pentanol
(11 µL; 0.1019 mmol) in benzene (1 mL) was stirred for 8 h at 80°C. After
removal of the solvent, the residue was treated with 780 µL of a solution
prepared from 0.5 g commercial HF·pyridine in 1.25 mL pyridine and 6.75
mL THF. After stirring for 24 h at RT, the reaction were quenched with a
phosphate buffer (pH 7.0; 10 mL), extracted with EtOAc (4×), dried
(Na2SO4) and concentrated. Purification by FC (25% acetone in hexanes).
(7S,9R,10S)-4,9-Dihydroxy-10-methyl-7-[(2E)-N-(pentyloxycarbonyl)-3-aminoprop-2-enyl]-7,8,9,10,11,12,13,14-octahydro-6-oxa-benzocyclodecen-5-one
(58). According to the procedure described for the synthesis of carbamate
50, acyl azide S13 (15 mg, 0.02435 mmol) gave 4.7 mg of carbamate 58.
[α]D = -13.2 (c 0.24, MeOH); IR 3387, 2933, 1727, 1710, 1680, 1603, 1293,
1243, 1113 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD) δ 7.25 (1H, app.t, J = 7.6 Hz),
6.75 (1H, d, J = 8.4 Hz), 6.73 (1H, d, J = 7.6 Hz), 6.44 (1H, d, J = 14.0
Hz), 5.14-5.22 (1H, m), 5.05 (1H, app.dt, J = 7.6, 14.0 Hz), 4.04 (2H, t,
J = 6.4 Hz), 3.82-3.88 (1H, m), 3.66 (1H, ddd, 3.6, 12.4, 12.4 Hz), 2.39
(2H, app.t, J = 6.6 Hz), 2.21 (1H, ddd, J = 6.4, 12.4, 12.4 Hz),
2.10-2.20 (1H, m), 1.40-1.80 (9H, m), 1.30-1.40 (5H, m), 0.95 (3H, d, J =
6.8 Hz), 0.92 (3H, t, J = 6.4 Hz); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CD3OD) δ 172.5,
162.3, 156.6, 147.0, 134.8, 128.5, 123.4, 116.3, 115.2, 105.5, 76.3,
66.4, 37.4, 34.4, 32.7, 29.9, 29.3, 23.5, 16.6, 14.5; MS (ES) m/z 448.20
([MH]+, 100), 470.19 ([MNa]+, 32). HRMS (FAB, MNBA, added LiI) Calcd for
C25H37NO6Li ([MLi]+): 454.2781. Found: 454.2779.
