$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM b. In the methanol-toluene mixture. Azide Vc, 1.1 g, was dissolved in a
mixture of 10 ml of toluene and 10 ml of methanol and refluxed with
stirring at 65°C. In the evacuated sample taken after 10 h of refluxing,
Methyl N-[3-(diethoxyphosphorylmethyl)furyl-2]-carbaminate (XVII) was
found as the main product. 1H NMR spectrum (CDCl3), δ, ppm.: 1.285 t
(CH3-ethyl, J HH 7.2 Hz), 2.817 d (CH2P, J HP 21.2 Hz), 3.699 s (CH3O),
6.288 br.s (H4-furan), 7.146 br.s (H5-furan), 7.890 br.s (NH); δP 26.407
