$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 3: To a solution of the acyl azide (2, 0.183 g, 0.159 mmol) in PhMe
(40 mL), was added the alcohol (70 uL, 0.398 mmol) and the reaction
mixtures was heated at reflux for 16 hrs. 3 g of SiO2 was added and all
solvents were evaporated. The solid was purified by flash chromatography,
eluting with MeOH/DCM (5-7 %) to provide 150 mg of an impure yellow
solid. The solid was re-purified by HPLC, eluting with ACN/H2O (5-95 %, 5
μM NH4CO2H). 10.2 mg of 16, a yellow solid. MS: m/z [M+H2O]+ 1287. LC: Rt
= 1.63 min. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6 , 400 MHz) δ ppm 9.0-8.8 (m, 2H), 8.48 (s, 1
H), 8.27-8.19 (m, 2 H), 8.16 (s, 1 H), 7.48 (s, 1 H), 7.37 (s, 1 H),
7.30-7.20 (m, 5 H), 5.55- 5.48 (m, 1 H), 5.40-5.25 (m, 1 H), 5.20-5.10
(m, 2 H), 5.07 (s, 2 H), 4.65-4.56 (m, 1 H), 4.38-4.33 (m, 2 H),
3.91-3.87 (m, 1 H), 3.80-3.75 (m, 2 H), 3.72-3.64 (m, 6 H), 3.56-3.52 (m,
2 H), 3.50 (2, 3 H), 3.36 (s, 3 H), 3.34-3.32 (m, 3 H), 2.84-2.78 (m, 1
H), 2.66 (s, 3 H), 2.57 (s, 3 H), 2.34-2.25 (m, 1 H), 2.05 (s, 2 H),
1.35-1.25 (m, 1 H), 1.04-1.00 (m, 3 H), 0.94-0.90 (m, 3 H). HRMS: m/z
[M+H]+ 1286.2864, C55H60N13O12S6, calc: 1286.2809.
