$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM [1-Phenylcycloprop-1-yl]isocyanate (9) To a solution of
1-phenyl-1-cyclopropanecarboxylic acid (1.02 g, 6.31 mmol) in toluene (30
mL) was added triethylamine (1.04 mL, 7.26 mmol). Diphenylphosphoryl
azide (1.41 mL, 6.56 mmol) was added dropwise and the mixture was heated
to reflux while stirring for 45 min. The mixture was then cooled to rt
and quenched with saturated aqueous NH4Cl (100 mL). After separation of
the two phases, the aqueous solution was extracted with Et2O (3 x 50 mL)
and the combined organic layers were washed with brine, dried with
anhydrous MgSO4 and concentrated in vacuo using a Kügelrohr apparatus.
The crude product 9 was dissolved in benzene (15 mL, 0.421 M), kept in
the freezer and used without purification in the next reaction. 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) : δ 7.38-7.24 (m, 5H), 1.37-1.20 (m, 4H); IR (neat/NaCl)
: 2922, 2845, 2265; LRMS (m/z (relative intensity)) : 159 (M+,62), 158
((M+-H), 100), 117 (65), 103 (90); HRMS calcd for C10H9ON: 159.0684,
found: 159.0679.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Curtius rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
