$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: This mixture was finally dissolved in dry THF
(40 mL) and cooled to 0 °C. A substechiometric amount of TiCl4 dissolved
in methylene chloride (approximately 0.5 mL of a 1.8 M solution) and Zn
dust (0.71 g, 10.9 mmol) were added in this sequence. The resulting
suspension was stirred overnight, while three more aliquots of catalyst
were added at regular intervals. The solid was then filtered over Celite
and the crude material extracted with 1 M HCl (20 mL) and brine (20 mL).
The organic phase was dried over magnesium sulfate, concentrated in
vacuo, and purified by flash chromatography (eluent: gradient from
EtOAc/PE 3:7 to EtOAc/PE 1:1) yielding 1.4 g (95%) of pure product.
Compound (+)-6 was obtained analogously. [α]20 D: +3.63 (c 2.00, CHCl3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stage 3 in the dark, stage 4 Curtius rearrangement, stage 6 incremental
addition of catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Novel Highly Selective Chiral Auxiliary for the Asymmetric Synthesis of
L- and D-α-Amino Acid Derivatives via a Multicomponent Ugi Reaction
