$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The crude yellow material of 2-hydroxy-5-nitrobenzoyl azide (22) (2.0 g,
0.009mol) was heated in toluene (50mL) under reflux for 10 h. The solvent
was removed from the reaction mixture at 25 °C under reduced pressure to
get an yellow solid as a mixture of two products, 23 and
5-nitro-2-hydroxyphenyl isocyanate (24); its IR spectrum (as KBr pellet)
showed absorptions at 3350-3380 (br.), 2160, and 1680-1710 cm-1 . 1H NMR
spectrum analyses for two sets of protons corresponded to two compounds
in a ~1:1 ratio. 5-nitrobenz[d]isoxazol-3(2H)-one (23);
5-nitro-2-hydroxyphenyl isocyanate (24) Set I: δ 8.51 (d, Jm 3.6Hz), 7.76
(dd, Jo 9.0Hz, Jm 2.8Hz), and 6.89 (d, Jo 9.0Hz) for the protons attached
to C-4, C-6, and C-7 respectively of 5-nitrobenz[d]isoxazol-3(2H)-one
(23). Set II: δ 7.44 (s), 7.55 (distorted d) and 6.16 (d, Jo 9.0Hz)
corresponded to 5-nitro-2-hydroxyphenyl isocyanate (24).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM 1:1 product ratio
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Benz[d]oxazolones Involving Concomitant Acetyl Migration
from Oxygen to Nitrogen
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ray, Sibdas; Ghosh, Sukla
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2010), 40(16), 2377-2388

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME451 STEP1
$RXN



